To expand the activation feature from supporting only the admin role to also fully supporting academic-head and system-administration roles with 100% functionality and zero errors, we need to make specific updates to:
 * admin-home.js (to remove the restriction blocking other roles and dynamically query separate or unified pre-approved collections/fields if needed, or handle them cleanly).
 * Firestore.rules (to ensure proper security permissions for reading pre-approved collections for academic heads and system administrators without triggering missing or insufficient permissions errors).
Let's evaluate the exact blocks to change.
Part 1: Updating admin-home.js
In your current admin-home.js, you have this restriction block under the activation listener:
  // 1. Restrict activation strictly to 'admin' role for now
  if (role !== 'admin') {
    alert('Activation is currently only available for Admin roles. Academic head and System administration activation will be enabled soon.');
    return;
  }

We need to remove this restriction so that academic-head and system-administration can proceed. Furthermore, we should route them to their respective Firestore collections (academic_heads and system_admins, or handle them dynamically based on the selected role) so their profiles land in the correct database collection just like admins.
